From: afni-win
Subject: [PATCH] thd_mastery: start 3dcalc with posix_spawnp instead of fork+execvp

Why the compat layer cannot handle this: fork() returns twice (in the parent
and in the child). A library on Windows cannot create a copy of the running
process, so fork() is not provided by the layer at all, and every call site
must be changed. This site only runs 3dcalc and waits for it, which is exactly
what posix_spawnp()+waitpid() do; the layer implements both with
CreateProcess/WaitForSingleObject. The change is POSIX and also works on
Linux and macOS.

diff --git a/src/thd_mastery.c b/src/thd_mastery.c
index 9c0a7b0..767ab28 100644
--- a/src/thd_mastery.c
+++ b/src/thd_mastery.c
@@ -479,6 +479,8 @@ ENTRY("THD_setup_mastery") ;
 
 #include <sys/types.h>
 #include <sys/wait.h>
+#include <spawn.h>
+#include <errno.h>
 
 static THD_3dim_dataset * THD_open_3dcalc( char *pname )
 {
@@ -553,22 +555,15 @@ ENTRY("THD_open_3dcalc") ;
    fprintf(stderr,"\n") ;
 #endif
 
-   child_pid = fork() ;
+   ii = posix_spawnp( &child_pid , "3dcalc" , NULL , NULL , newArgv , environ ) ;
 
-   if( child_pid == (pid_t)(-1) ){
-     perror("*** Can't fork 3dcalc()") ;
+   if( ii != 0 ){
+     errno = ii ;
+     perror("*** Can't spawn 3dcalc()") ;
      for( ii=0 ; ii < newArgc-1 ; ii++ ) free(newArgv[ii]) ;
      free(newArgv) ; RETURN(NULL) ;
    }
 
-   if( child_pid == 0 ){  /*-- I'm the child --*/
-
-     execvp( "3dcalc" , newArgv ) ;        /* should not return */
-     perror("*** Can't execvp 3dcalc()") ;
-     _exit(1) ;
-
-   }
-
    /*-- I'm the parent --*/
 
    STATUS("Waiting for 3dcalc() process to run") ;
